    {
      "id": "f6ngpw0",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Sources of Ancient Indian History"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Ancient Indian History relies on literary, archaeological, numismatic, and foreign account sources.",
        "The Prehistoric Period spans the Paleolithic, Mesolithic, Neolithic, and Chalcolithic eras.",
        "The Indus Valley Civilization (Harappan Civilization) is celebrated for sophisticated town planning, advanced drainage systems, and burnt brick construction.",
        "Key sites include Harappa, Mohenjo-daro, Lothal, Kalibangan, and Dholavira, each contributing unique cultural and economic evidence.",
        "The Harappan economy thrived on agriculture, craft specialization, standardization of weights, and foreign trade with Mesopotamia."
      ],
      "id": "f7mg3um"
    },
    {
